    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Cognitive-Science-and-Computer-Science_JR2026316": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Cognitive Science and Computer Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Assistant Professor of Cognitive Science and Computer Science Job Description: Barnard seeks to hire a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cognitive Science and Computer Science to begin July 1, 2027. The area of focus is at the intersection of Human Cognition and Artificial Intelligence. The faculty member's primary affiliation and tenure line will be in the Department of Computer Science, with responsibilities split between the Computer Science Department and the Cognitive Science Program at Barnard. We are seeking candidates who work at the intersection of human cognition and artificial intelligence. The ideal candidate will pursue research and teaching that advances both our understanding of how the mind works and the development of new cognitively inspired and ethically designed AI systems. A successful hire will further the aims and vision of the Cognitive Science Program and Computer Science Department at Barnard. Barnard is a premier liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City affiliated with Columbia University. Barnard faculty are expected to engage in teaching, research, curriculum and program development, undergraduate advising, and mentoring of undergraduate research. There are also opportunities to collaborate with faculty and students across Barnard College and Columbia University, including Columbia’s NSF AI Institute for Artificial and Natural Intelligence (https://arni-institute.org/). The Program in Cognitive Science at Barnard (https://barnard.edu/cogsci) is a relatively new program that brings together faculty across several departments, including Psychology, Philosophy, Neuroscience and Behavior, Computer Science, and Economics. Barnard’s Computer Science (CS) Department (https://cs.barnard.edu/) has faculty with expertise in Security and Privacy, Natural Language Processing, Computer Graphics, Augmented Reality, AI and Law, Human-Computer Interaction, and Programming Synthesis. The Barnard Computer Science Department works closely with the Vagelos Computational Science Center and with the Columbia CS Department (https://www.cs.columbia.edu/). Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD in Computer Science, Cognitive Science or a related discipline, and should have a promising research agenda and record of scholarship, as well as a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching, mentoring, and increasing participation in cognitive science and/or computer science. Application Requirements Applicants are required to upload the following documents. Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered. Curriculum Vitae   (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover Letter summarizing interest in and preparation for this particular position Research statement highlighting past accomplishments and future plans Teaching and mentoring statement describing teaching and mentoring philosophy, experiences, and interests The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting , please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information, please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible. Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email.  Review of applications will begin on approximately November 2, 2026 and may continue until the position is filled. For questions or further information about the position please contact cogsci-cs-search@barnard.edu. For technical questions on submitting your Workday application please contact workday@barnard.edu. Salary: $95,000 - $140,000 Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Professional-Practice-in-Theatre_JR2026223": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Theatre",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Theatre The Department of Theatre at Barnard College seeks a full-time Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in design: a working theatre designer with expertise in design and in the pedagogy of design teaching, to start July 1, 2027. Applicants are expected to hold the appropriate terminal degree (MFA) in design and possess an exciting portfolio of design work in theatre. Competitive candidates will have a record of professional productions and be competent in two design areas. We have a particular need for scenic design, and a strong interest in candidates with expertise in costume, lighting, or sound design as well as interest in video and projection design, props design, or puppetry. Competitive applicants are likely to have a demonstrated interest and facility with sustainable theatre practices. The candidate would be expected to contribute to service at the departmental and eventually college-wide level. PoPP appointments require ongoing artistic work for retention and promotion. The successful candidate must develop, sustain, and advance a nationally-visible artistic trajectory throughout their appointment. Job Description: The Department of Theatre at Barnard College, Columbia University, seeks a full-time Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in design -- a working theatre designer with expertise in design and in the pedagogy of design teaching -- to start July 1, 2027. Applicants are expected to hold the appropriate terminal degree (MFA) in design and possess an exciting portfolio of design work in theatre.  In addition to an MFA, applicants might also hold the Ph.D. and so be qualified to teach more traditionally research-oriented courses, e.g. history of scenic design, critical history of fashion and costume design. Competitive candidates will have a record of professional productions and be competent in two design areas.  We have a particular need for scenic design, and a strong interest in candidates with expertise in costume, lighting, or sound design as well as interest in video and projection design, props design, or puppetry.  Competitive applicants are likely to have a demonstrated interest and facility with sustainable theatre practices. As a full time reviewed and renewable position, we expect the successful candidate to participate fully in the life of a dynamic Theatre department that places equal weight on lecture/seminar courses and practicum courses. The candidate would be expected to contribute to service at the departmental and eventually college-wide level. Assistant Professor of Professional Practice appointments require—in analogy to tenure-track faculty—ongoing artistic work for retention and promotion. The successful candidate must develop, sustain, and advance a nationally-visible artistic trajectory during the first seven years of appointment (to be considered for promotion) and beyond. The Department of Theatre at Barnard College offers the undergraduate Theatre major to all Barnard College, Columbia College, and Columbia School of General Studies students. The teaching load is four courses per year, with accompanying undergraduate advising, service on departmental committees, and service to the College. We expect the person hired into this position to design 1-2 main stage shows per year, co-advise the annual Thesis Festival, and take on the oversight and mentoring of the senior thesis in design, in which 2-5 students per year design in one of four areas for a main stage production, in collaboration with a professional director and design team.  Salary: $95,000 - $115,000 Review of applications will begin on approximately October 25, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions or further information please contact theatredesignsearch@barnard.edu. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications MFA in Theatre design 3-5 years professional work Competency in teaching 2 design areas Application Requirements Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered.  Applicants are required to upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae  (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover letter summarizing interest in, and preparation for, this particular position Teaching and mentoring statement describing your teaching philosophy Digital design portfolio, maximum 40 pages The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting, please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information, please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible. Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify at least three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email. Barnard is a premier liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City affiliated with Columbia University. Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Lecturer-of-Biological-Sciences_JR2026296": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Lecturer of Biological Sciences Barnard is a premier liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City affiliated with Columbia University. Job Description: The Department of Biology at Barnard College, Columbia University, seeks a full-time Lecturer, starting July 2027, with a specialization in Computational Biology. The teaching load for this position is 6 courses per year. Teaching duties include lecture and laboratory sections of Introduction to Cell and Molecular Biology and upper-level lecture and laboratory courses in Computational Biology. We encourage applications from candidates working in plant biology, biodiversity broadly defined, epidemiology, genomics, systems biology, protein structural biology, and biological data science. As a full-time reviewed and renewable position, we expect Lecturers to participate fully in the life of the department and college, including advising, mentoring, service, and leadership. Lecturers are reviewed in their third year of full-time service, with the possibility for reappointment and consideration for promotion to Senior Lecturer in the seventh year. Subsequent reviews typically occur on a seven-year cycle. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications A Ph.D. is required. Prior experience or demonstrated commitment to teaching and mentoring diverse students is desirable. Application Requirements Applicants are required to upload the following documents. Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered. Curriculum Vitae   (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover letter summarizing interest in, and preparation for, the position. Research/Scholarship statement highlighting how the applicant’s research experience will inform their teaching. Teaching and mentoring statement describing the upper-level lab and lecture courses the applicant could teach (both existing offerings and new courses). The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting , please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information , please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible. Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email.  Review of applications will begin on approximately November 15, 2026 and may continue until the position is filled. The search committee plans to conduct Zoom interviews with semi-finalists in December. Campus visits will be conducted in January and February. For questions about the position, pleaser contact biologyjobcomp@barnard.edu. For technical questions on submitting your Workday application please contact workday@barnard.edu. Salary: $88,000 - $94,000 Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
