    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Dance_JR2026294": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Dance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Assistant Professor of Dance The Department of Dance at Barnard College, Columbia University in New York City, seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Dance with a focus on Global Dance Studies. This research-focused position emphasizes scholarship and coursework in dance history, theory, and cultural studies. Job Description: Barnard is a premier liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City affiliated with Columbia University. The Barnard College Department of Dance, located in a world dance capital, offers an interdisciplinary program that integrates the study of dance within a liberal arts setting of intellectual and creative exploration. The Dance Major builds upon practice and performance with accomplished artists, and a rich array of Dance Studies courses with outstanding research scholars, allowing students' creative work to develop in dialogue with critical inquiry into the history, culture, theory, and forms of western and non-western performance, typically enhanced by study in other disciplines. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications We seek candidates whose area of interest or specialization includes East Asian, South Asian, African or African Diasporic, Indigenous, Pacific Islander and Native Hawaiian Dance Studies, or dance studies of the Americas. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in dance or related discipline at time of appointment, a distinguished record of scholarly publication or promise of such, proven capacity for teaching excellence at the college level, and ability and desire to perform service within the department, college, and university. This appointment will be based in the Department of Dance, with potential affiliation in a relevant Department as appropriate. Candidates may also be eligible to join the faculty of the Columbia University Ph.D. Program in Theatre and Performance. Application Requirements Applicants are required to upload the following documents. Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered. Curriculum Vitae   (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover Letter summarizing interest in, and preparation for, the position Research statement highlighting past accomplishments and future plans Teaching and mentoring statement describing teaching and mentoring philosophy, experiences, and interests Two writing examples, preferably published articles and book chapters The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting , please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information , please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible. Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email.  Review of applications will begin on approximately October 30, 2026 and may continue until the position is filled. For questions or further information about the position please contact DanceAsstProfSearch@barnard.edu. For technical questions on submitting your Workday application please contact workday@barnard.edu. Salary: $95,000 - $115,000 Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Lecturer-of-Philosophy_JR2026295": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Philosophy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Lecturer of Philosophy The Barnard College Department of Philosophy invites applications for a full-time lecturer position to begin July 1, 2027. Barnard is a premier liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City affiliated with Columbia University. The Barnard College and Columbia University Philosophy Departments function as a single department for most academic matters. Job Description: The teaching load is 3+3 courses per year. Non-teaching duties include advising undergraduate students and participating in service at the departmental and college levels. The successful candidate will be able to teach introductory and advanced courses, as well as develop new classes that draw on the candidate’s specific areas of specialization and competence. While these areas are open, the successful candidate must be able to teach Introduction to Logic. Lecturers are reviewed in their third year of full-time service, with the possibility for reappointment and consideration for promotion to Senior Lecturer in the seventh year; subsequent reviews typically occur on a seven-year cycle. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Philosophy by time of appointment, or no later that Fall 2027. Application Requirements Applicants are required to upload the following documents. Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered. Curriculum Vitae   (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover letter stating interest, preparation, and qualification for this position. While the cover letter should primarily speak to a candidate's teaching background and interests, it may also speak to the candidate's academic or professional accomplishments and future plans. Evidence of teaching effectiveness including: a teaching statement describing teaching philosophy, experiences, and interests, at least 3 sample syllabi, recent teaching evaluations (if available) A writing sample of 10-30 pages Research statement (Optional) The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting , please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information , please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible. Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email.  Review of applications will begin on approximately October 30, 2026 and may continue until the position is filled. For questions or further information about the position please contact philosophysearch@barnard.edu . For technical questions on submitting your Workday application please contact workday@barnard.edu. Salary: $88,000 - $94,000 Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Herbert-and-Florence-Irving-Professor-of-Biology-or-Biophysics--and-Professor-of-Chemistry_JR5876": {
      "title": "Herbert and Florence Irving Professor of Biology or Biophysics, and Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Herbert and Florence Irving Professor of Biology or Biophysics, and Professor of Chemistry The Barnard College Department of Chemistry seeks an innovative individual whose research contributes to understanding and curing cancer to serve as the inaugural Herbert and Florence Irving Professor of Biology or Biophysics and Professor of Chemistry. This will be an open rank search. Special consideration for this endowed position will be given to candidates working in the field of chemical biology. Applicants must have a PhD degree in chemistry, biochemistry, chemical biology, or a related discipline, a dedication to undergraduate education both in the classroom and laboratory, and a research program that furthers the understanding and treatment of cancer. Postdoctoral experience is strongly preferred. Responsibilities include teaching in the biochemistry or organic chemistry course sequences, with special consideration given to those who can teach in both. Job Description: The Barnard College Department of Chemistry seeks an innovative individual whose research contributes to understanding and curing cancer to serve as the inaugural Herbert and Florence Irving Professor of Biology or Biophysics, and Professor of Chemistry. This will be an open rank search, and we are prepared to appoint at the assistant, associate, or full professor rank. Special consideration for this endowed position will be given to candidates working in the field of chemical biology. The successful applicant will be eligible to join the Herbert Irving Comprehensive Cancer Center (HICCC) and/or the Irving Institute for Cancer Dynamics (IICD) at Columbia University.  Barnard College is an independent liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City, affiliated with Columbia University. The Barnard Chemistry department currently consists of eight tenure-line faculty, three lecturers, a core facilities and laboratory instrument manager, a senior associate laboratory director, and three lab instructional specialists. Barnard faculty are expected to engage in research as well as undergraduate curriculum development, teaching, advising, and research mentoring. The standard teaching load for a tenure-line faculty member is two courses per semester. This may include advanced electives as well as introductory courses. For this position, special consideration will be given to applicants who can teach in the biochemistry and organic chemistry course sequences.  Barnard College is located in the vibrant Morningside Heights neighborhood, adjacent to Columbia University’s main campus, and approximately 2.5 miles south of Columbia’s medical campus. In late 2026, all of the physical and life sciences departments will move into the newly renovated Roy and Diana Vagelos Science Center, where the person in this position will have a 740-square-foot lab with adjoining office, and access to ample shared resources and equipment on the Barnard campus. Barnard’s status as a highly selective liberal arts college affiliated with a major research university uniquely enables its faculty to innovate in both research and pedagogy. Review of applications will begin about September 15, 2026 and may continue until the position is filled. Salary: $100,000 to $250,000 For questions or further information please contact Christina Vizcarra at cvizcarr@barnard.edu. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications Applicants must have a PhD degree in chemistry, biochemistry, chemical biology, or a related discipline, a dedication to undergraduate education both in the classroom and laboratory, and a research program that furthers the understanding and treatment of cancer. Postdoctoral experience is strongly preferred.  Application Requirements Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered.  Applicants are required to upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae  (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover letter summarizing interest in, and preparation for, this particular position Statement describing teaching and mentoring philosophy, experiences, and interests, including where the candidate envisions teaching within the chemistry curriculum Research/scholarship statement The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting, please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information, please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible.  Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify at least three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email. Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Assistant-Professor-of-Neuroscience---Behavior_JR2026184": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neuroscience & Behavior",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Assistant Professor of Neuroscience & Behavior The Department of Neuroscience and Behavior at Barnard College, Columbia University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position, beginning July 2027. The successful candidate will establish an innovative, externally funded research program in neuroscience. We are especially interested in candidates whose research advances our understanding of the mechanisms underlying learning and memory across levels of analysis. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, the cellular, molecular, systems, or behavioral mechanisms of learning, memory encoding, consolidation, retrieval, developmental or lifespan changes in learning and memory, or neurological or psychiatric disorders. Candidates employing computational, behavioral, systems, cellular, molecular, or other integrative approaches are encouraged to apply.  Job Description: Barnard is a premier liberal arts undergraduate college for women in New York City affiliated with Columbia University. Barnard faculty are members of the vibrant Columbia University neuroscience community. They have extensive opportunities for collaboration across the university and New York City, including at the Zuckerman Institute, Columbia University Irving Medical Center, and the New York State Psychiatric Institute. The Neuroscience and Behavior Department occupies a new state-of-the-art research facility. Teaching responsibilities include four courses per year. The successful candidate will contribute to the Neuroscience and Behavior curriculum and will have the opportunity to develop courses aligned with their expertise, including learning and memory, behavioral neuroscience, systems neuroscience, cognitive neuroscience, computational neuroscience, or related fields. We are especially interested in candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring and with experience or strong potential for engaging undergraduate researchers from diverse backgrounds.    Salary: $95,000 - $115,000       Review of applications will begin on approximately November 15, 2026 and may continue until the position is filled. The search committee plans to conduct Zoom interviews with semi-finalists around mid to late November 2026. Campus visits will be conducted around December 2026. For questions, contact neurosearch@barnard.edu. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications A Ph.D. and postdoctoral experience are required; teaching experience is desirable and will be considered in the evaluation of candidates. Application Requirements Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered.  Applicants are required to upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae  (maximum file size: 5 MB) A single file (maximum file size: 30 MB) containing: Cover letter summarizing interest in and preparation for this particular position Teaching and mentoring statement that also addresses ability to work effectively with a student population that is broadly diverse Statement of research and scholarship interests Two representative publications The accepted file formats are: CSV, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PDF, PNG, XLS, XLSX. Files in other formats may not be readable and may not be considered during the review process. Before submitting , please review the file containing your application materials to ensure that all information is complete and correct. Application materials cannot be edited after submission. To submit new or updated materials and information , please withdraw your original application and submit a new one as soon as possible. Only semi-finalists will be asked to identify at least three references. Referees will receive an email notification instructing them to upload confidential letters of recommendation within one week of receipt of the email. Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability. Qualified candidates of diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow---Environmental-Science_JR2026106": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow, \tEnvironmental Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Environmental Science Professor Mike He is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Environmental Health at Barnard College, a premier liberal arts college in Manhattan affiliated with Columbia University. Reporting to Dr. He as Principal Investigator, the Postdoctoral Research Fellow is responsible for conducting research in environmental epidemiology and exposure assessment, specifically on the effects of environmental mixtures on immunological outcomes in children. Duties include manuscript preparation and data analysis on all aims of the project. Additionally, the Postdoctoral Fellow will serve as a teaching assistant and assist with the preparation of new grant applications. Job Description: Professor Mike He is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Environmental Health at Barnard College, a premier liberal arts college in Manhattan affiliated with Columbia University. Duties and Responsibilities: Construct air pollution and meteorological data prediction models using machine-learning based methods Conduct epidemiologic analyses studying associations of environmental mixtures on immune-based outcomes in children Train on and implement advanced statistical methods in environmental health Assist with teaching courses at Barnard, including serving as Teaching Assistant and Guest Lecturers Prepare and lead the write-up of manuscripts associated with the conducted research Mentor undergraduate and graduate-level research assistants Assist with the preparation of new grant applications Direct supervision of fairly routine work following standard practices or policies. This job description is intended as a summary of the primary responsibilities of and qualifications of this position. The job description is not intended as inclusive of all duties an individual in this position might be asked to perform or of all qualifications that may be required either now or in the future. This is a grant-funded position for one year with the possibility of renewal. Salary: $72,000 Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications: PhD in Environmental Health (or related field) Advanced mastery of statistical programming in R/Python (or equivalent) Strong data analysis/data management skills Excellent written communication skills and experience with manuscript/grant writing Ability to work independently Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience in machine-learning based prediction modeling Background in statistics, computer science, and/or immunology a plus Application Requirements: Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered. Applicants are required to upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae (maximum file size: 5 MB) Cover letter describing research interests, relevant experience, and professional goals Finalists will be asked to identify three references. For inquiries about this position, please contact Dr. Mike He ( mhe@barnard.edu ) Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis.  Qualified candidates of all backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Full time"
    },
    "https://barnard.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/New-York-City-NY/Adjunct-Associate--Art-History_JR5652": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Art History",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current Barnard College employee, please use the internal career site to apply for this position. Job: Adjunct Lecturer, Art History The Art History Department at Barnard College seeks a part-time instructor to teach the following undergraduate courses during the 2026-2027 academic year: Fall 2026: AHIS BC2525 Lecture Modern Japanese Art History. Job Description: The Art History Department at Barnard College seeks a part-time instructor to teach the following undergraduate courses during the 2026-2027 academic year: Fall 2026:  AHIS BC2525 Lecture Modern Japanese Art History. Pay Rate: $14,000 This appointment may include work performed outside of the classroom, including course preparation, attendance at meetings, course assessment, grading assignments and exams, as well as the resolution of incomplete or disputed grades. Skills, Qualifications & Requirements: Required Qualifications Terminal degree in a related discipline, with all requirements for the degree completed by the time of hiring offer.   Application Requirements Only complete applications submitted via Workday will be considered.  Applicants are required to upload the following documents: CV Statement of interest (including teaching philosophy, most relevant prior teaching experience, advanced pedagogical or relevant training) Finalists will be asked to identify three references, including one with direct knowledge of their teaching capabilities.    Barnard College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Barnard does not discriminate due to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender and/or gender identity or expression, marital or parental status, national origin, ethnicity, citizenship status, veteran or military status, age, disability, or any other legally protected basis, and to the extent permitted by law. Qualified candidates of diverse ethnic and racial backgrounds are encouraged to apply for vacant positions at all levels. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, and training. The above hiring range represents the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Company: Barnard College Time Type: Part time"
    }
